# Beorn's Hospitality: "Landfall - Whenever a land you control enters, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.
# {5}{G}{G}: This enchantment becomes a Bear creature in addition to its other types and gains 'This creature's power and
# toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.' (This effect doesn't end.)" On turn 1 the enchantment is no
# creature, so the Ornithopter is the only target of the Forest's landfall (a +1/+1 counter, the enchantment getting none). Bot2's
# Island on turn 2 triggers nothing. On turn 3 the ability costs exactly seven mana: it becomes an Enchantment Creature - Bear
# sized by Bot1's lands only (1/1, Bot2's Island not counted). It stays a creature through the end of turn (it doesn't end,
# CR 611.2a) and on turn 5 a Plains makes it a legal target of its own landfall: two lands, a +1/+1 counter on top (CR 613.4c): 3/3.

